# Tailwind CSS v4 Conventions

## Design Tokens via `@theme`

Brand colours are declared in `src/app/globals.css` inside a `@theme` block.
This registers them as native Tailwind utilities — no `(--*)` wrapper needed.

```css
/* globals.css */
@theme {
  --color-ink: #050505;
  --color-primary: #b7d5eb;
  --color-primary-subtle: #eef7fc;
  --color-primary-muted: #d8eaf6;
  --color-secondary: #1f2528;
  --color-surface: #f5f3ef;
  --color-border: #d8d8d2;
}
```

## Using Tokens in Components

Because they are `@theme` tokens, use them like any built-in Tailwind colour:

```tsx
// Correct — plain utility name
<div className="bg-ink text-primary ring-1 ring-border" />
<p className="text-secondary/65" />
<span className="bg-primary-subtle hover:bg-primary-muted" />

// Wrong — do not use (--*) for @theme colours
<div className="bg-(--color-ink)" />          // ✗
<div className="bg-[var(--color-ink)]" />     // ✗
```

## Token Reference

| Utility class | CSS variable | Hex | Role |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ink` | `--color-ink` | `#050505` | Near-black — headings, dark surfaces |
| `primary` | `--color-primary` | `#b7d5eb` | Brand accent blue |
| `primary-subtle` | `--color-primary-subtle` | `#eef7fc` | Light primary background |
| `primary-muted` | `--color-primary-muted` | `#d8eaf6` | Primary hover state |
| `secondary` | `--color-secondary` | `#1f2528` | Body text, labels |
| `surface` | `--color-surface` | `#f5f3ef` | Page and card backgrounds |
| `border` | `--color-border` | `#d8d8d2` | Dividers, rings |

## Opacity Modifiers

Works the same as built-in colours:

```tsx
text-secondary/65      // 65% opacity
ring-primary/30        // 30% opacity ring
bg-primary/12          // 12% opacity background
```

## No Arbitrary `rem` or `em` in Components

Never use `[Xrem]` or `[Xem]` as arbitrary values in JSX class strings.

```tsx
// Wrong
rounded-[2rem]
tracking-[0.2em]
text-[0.65rem]
gap-[1.5rem]

// Correct — use built-in scale
rounded-4xl        // 2rem
text-sm            // 0.875rem
gap-6              // 1.5rem

// Correct — define a named @theme token for values with no built-in
tracking-label     // defined in globals.css @theme as --tracking-label: 0.2em
```

**Rule:** if no built-in Tailwind class covers the value, add a named token to
`@theme` in `src/app/globals.css`, then reference it by name in components.
The em/rem lives in CSS — not in JSX strings.

## Design Token Reference

### Colours

| Utility | CSS variable | Hex | Role |
|---|---|---|---|
| `ink` | `--color-ink` | `#050505` | Near-black — headings, dark surfaces |
| `primary` | `--color-primary` | `#b7d5eb` | Brand accent blue |
| `primary-subtle` | `--color-primary-subtle` | `#eef7fc` | Light primary background |
| `primary-muted` | `--color-primary-muted` | `#d8eaf6` | Primary hover state |
| `secondary` | `--color-secondary` | `#1f2528` | Body text, labels |
| `surface` | `--color-surface` | `#f5f3ef` | Page and card backgrounds |
| `border` | `--color-border` | `#d8d8d2` | Dividers, rings |

### Letter-spacing

| Utility | CSS variable | Value | Usage |
|---|---|---|---|
| `tracking-label-sm` | `--tracking-label-sm` | `0.15em` | Small controls labels |
| `tracking-label` | `--tracking-label` | `0.2em` | Standard uppercase section labels |
| `tracking-label-lg` | `--tracking-label-lg` | `0.24em` | Wide brand label in header |

## When `(--*)` Is Still Correct

Only use `(--*)` for CSS variables that are **not** in `@theme` — for example,
one-off values defined in `:root` or inline styles you cannot express as a
Tailwind utility.

## Arbitrary Values — Allowed Cases

`[]` is still appropriate for layout values that are not design tokens:

```tsx
grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]    // fractional grid ratios — no token needed
max-w-[theme(spacing.prose)] // theme() references
```
